Z||000008||rogergarrison||07-20-2001||03:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTMike:<BR><B>whos paul harvey??    well the  package sayid it can be used on heads and all other stuff on an engien including manafolds.    and its good up to 600*   its all hardend up now so i'm off to put it back on .    i'll tell you how long it lasts</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <P>thats on 'normal' car manifold. Fiero exhaust system gets as high as 1200* look at them at night in the dark. I even tried aircraft jet engine paint, only stayed on a few weeks before cooking off. and it said good to 1500*<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||07-20-2001||04:16 PM||||whats the worst that can happen here<BR> <BR>the epoxy will melt and the vacuum from the intake plenium will suck it into the motor<P> and there will be melted epoxy glue in the intake valves, in the pistons, maybe in the rings<P>  I guess that might be bad.<P>   might want to keep an eye on it when you first start it up - see if the epoxy gets soft.||||reg||1
Z||000010||StuGood||07-20-2001||06:03 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>...Fiero exhaust system gets as high as 1200* look at them at night in the dark...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Even if the exhaust gets to 1200F, the EGR tube sure doesn't - at least not the plenum end.  If the (aluminum) plenum ever got to 1200F, it would get kinda, well, liquid   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">.<P>Sounds like some kind of drain unclogger, doesn't it?  "Oh, no! - the sinks clogged again - do we have any Liquid Plenum left?"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||GTMike||07-20-2001||06:15 PM||||well its on and i ran it all day in town  in 90 degree weather and its fine.   thanks for the concern. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||07-20-2001||08:23 PM||||just being on the safe side since Fieros burn so ez to start with. The EGR tube is just above the crossover pipe so sure it dont get as hot as the pipes themselves. and yes I know the plenum doesnt glow red like them. What makes the tubes fail in the first place is movement and exposure to high heat, and being made out of such cheap crap.||||reg||1
Z||000013||ka4nkf||07-20-2001||11:05 PM||||Good luck, but I put a little JB on the exhaust manifold just to see what would happen. I let it set for 24 hours. when I started the engine it had run less than 1 minute when the JB started smoking and stinking. It was all burned off in less than 2 minutes. the stink was bad. JB is good but it won't take this kind of heat, and that EGR tube does get hot.||||reg||1
